{"count":1095,"next":null,"previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=10&page_size=100","results":[{"id":1206,"title":"AFP captures NPA firearm in Masbate","slug":"afp-captures-npa-firearm-in-masbate","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) captured a high-powered firearm after an encounter with the communist terrorist New People's Army (NPA) in Masbate on April 18.</p>\r\n<p>Operating troops from Philippine Army's 2nd Infantry Battalion (2IB), while conducting combat operations, encountered more or less 15 NPAs at the boundary of Sitio Buntod, Brgy. Buenasuerte and Brgy. Lampuyang both of Pio V. Corpuz, Masbate.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-19T21:02:41+08:00","hits":256},{"id":1207,"title":"3 terrorist NPAs yield in Masbate","slug":"3-terrorist-npas-yield-in-masbate","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Three communist terrorist NPAs (CNTs) yielded to the Philippine Army’s 2nd Infantry Battalion (2IB) of the 9th Infantry Division in Masbate on April 21, 2022.</p>\r\n<p>According to Lt. Col. Siegfried Felipe F Awichen, Commanding Officer of 2IB, after a series of negotiation, his troops was able to convince Alias Pinoy, Alias Darwin, and Alias Nikoy to lay down their arms and heed the government’s call for peace by availing the Enhanced Comprehensive Local Integration Program (E-CLIP) of the government.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-19T08:09:52+08:00","hits":264},{"id":1208,"title":"2 terrorist NPAs killed in Quezon encounter","slug":"2-terrorist-npas-killed-in-quezon-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Two communist terrorist NPAs (CNTs) were killed in an encounter with government troops in Quezon province on April 18.</p>\r\n<p>While conducting security operations at Sito Angelo, Barangay Umiray, General Nakar on Monday afternoon, troops from the Philippine Army's 24th Division Reconnaissance Company under the 2nd Infantry Division chanced upon the more or less seven CNTs, resulting in a firefight.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-19T08:06:05+08:00","hits":245},{"id":1209,"title":"JUSMAG Chief exit call to CSAFP","slug":"jusmag-chief-exit-call-to-csafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04192022 JUSMAG Chief exit call to CSAFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"535\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04192022 JUSMAG Chief exit call to CSAFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>EXIT CALL | Colonel Stephen C Ma, United States Army, the Senior Defense Attaché Officer and Chief of the Joint U.S. Military Assistance Group-Philippines, made an exit call to the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), General Andres C Centino at the General Headquarters Building, Camp Aguinaldo on April 19.</p>\r\n<p>Colonel Ma started his exit call to key officials of the AFP before his term as defense attaché and JUSMAG-PH Chief ends in May 2022. He previously met with Major General Romulo A Manuel Jr, the Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence, J2, AFP. (Photo: A2C Castro PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04192022%20JUSMAG%20Chief%20exit%20call%20to%20CSAFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-19T08:02:36+08:00","hits":424},{"id":1210,"title":"AFP seizes NPA firearms in Oriental Mindoro","slug":"afp-seizes-npa-firearms-in-oriental-mindoro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) seized two high-powered firearms and other war materiel after an encounter with the communist terrorist New People's Army (NPA) in Oriental Mindoro on Sunday, April 17.</p>\r\n<p>Operating troops from Philippine Army's 76th Infantry Battalion (76IB) acted on a report from concerned civilians that armed men were threatening the residents at their farms when they encountered more or less eight CNTs at Sitio Pitong Gatang, Brgy. Manguyang in Gloria, Oriental Mindoro. The firefight lasted for about ten minutes, after which the enemy scampered in different directions.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-18T20:59:54+08:00","hits":198},{"id":1211,"title":"AFP foils NPA extortion attempt in Laguna","slug":"afp-foils-npa-extortion-attempt-in-laguna","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) prevented the communist terrorist group (CTG) extortion activity in Laguna as soldiers encountered them on Sunday, April 17.</p>\r\n<p>According to Lt. Col. Danilo V Escandor, some concerned citizens reported the presence of the armed group on their farms, extorting for food and money, which prompted the Philippine Army's 1st Infantry Battalion under the 2nd Infantry Division to conduct a security operation to verify the report.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-18T20:55:37+08:00","hits":4},{"id":1212,"title":"AFP intensifies relief operations in Leyte","slug":"afp-intensifies-relief-operations-in-leyte","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04182022 AFP intensifies relief operations in Leyte.jpg\" width=\"854\" height=\"578\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04182022 AFP intensifies relief operations in Leyte.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has intensified its humanitarian assistance and disaster response (HADR) operations in Leyte following the devastation caused by Typhoon Agaton.</p>\r\n<p>The Visayas Command on Saturday announced that efforts will be sustained to provide needed assistance to alleviate the distress of people experiencing hardship brought about by the recent calamity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04182022%20AFP%20intensifies%20relief%20operations%20in%20Leyte.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-18T15:59:34+08:00","hits":293},{"id":1213,"title":"AFP seizes 22 firearms, dismantles NPA Guerilla Front 3","slug":"afp-seizes-22-firearms-dismantles-npa-guerilla-front-3","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04132022 AFP seizes 22 firearms dismantles NPA Guerilla Front 3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04132022 AFP seizes 22 firearms dismantles NPA Guerilla Front 3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) seized 22 high-powered firearms from the communist New People's Army terrorists (CNTs) in Agusan del Sur on Monday, April 11.</p>\r\n<p>The 60th Infantry Battalion of the Joint Task Force (JTF) Agila discovered 10 AK 47 rifles, seven M16 rifles, a light machine gun, M14 rifle, M79 grenade launcher, Garand rifle, and M16 rifle in Bagul River, Kasapa II, La Paz, Agusan Del Sur.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04132022%20AFP%20seizes%2022%20firearms%20dismantles%20NPA%20Guerilla%20Front%203.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-13T15:57:18+08:00","hits":180},{"id":1214,"title":"Commander of U.S. Pacific Air Forces visits AFP Headquarters","slug":"commander-of-u-s-pacific-air-forces-visits-afp-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 Commander of U.S. Pacific Air Forces visits AFP Headquarters.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 Commander of U.S. Pacific Air Forces visits AFP Headquarters.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Commander of the United States Pacific Air Forces (USPACAF) paid a courtesy call to the Acting Vice Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Tuesday, April 12.</p>\r\n<p>General Kenneth Wilsbach met with Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes at the Balangiga Hall, General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo. The two discussed potential areas of security cooperation between the AFP and USPACAF.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04122022%20AFP%20Chief%20thanks%20soldiers%20for%20highest%20approval%20trust%20ratings%20in%20latest%20survey.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-12T15:54:33+08:00","hits":216},{"id":1215,"title":"AFP Chief thanks soldiers for highest approval, trust ratings in latest survey","slug":"afp-chief-thanks-soldiers-for-highest-approval-trust-ratings-in-latest-survey","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 AFP Chief thanks soldiers for highest approval trust ratings in latest survey.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"536\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 AFP Chief thanks soldiers for highest approval trust ratings in latest survey.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) thanked the soldiers for the highest approval and trust ratings that the military garnered in the latest Publicus Asia survey.</p>\r\n<p>During his visit to the Philippine Army Headquarters in Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City, General Andres C Centino recognized the troop's contribution to the AFP campaign.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04122022%20AFP%20Chief%20thanks%20soldiers%20for%20highest%20approval%20trust%20ratings%20in%20latest%20survey.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-12T15:51:54+08:00","hits":256},{"id":1216,"title":"Statement on AFP garners Highest Trust and Approval Rating in 2022 Pahayag First Quarter Survey by Publicus Asia","slug":"statement-on-afp-garners-highest-trust-and-approval-rating-in-2022-pahayag-first-quarter-survey-by-publicus-asia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcome the Filipino people's continuous trust and confidence, as shown in the 2022 Pahayag First Quarter Survey by Publicus Asia.</p>\r\n<p>In the survey involving 1,500 respondents, the AFP garnered the highest approval and trust rating among government agencies, with 67.4% and 53.4% ratings, respectively.</p>\r\n<p>The survey result manifests our people's optimism with our unremitting efforts to secure peace and security, paving the way for the country's continuous development.</p>\r\n<p>The men and women of the AFP shall reciprocate this encouraging result with renewed dedication to perform our mandate of protecting the people and securing the state.</p>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-12T11:01:44+08:00","hits":290},{"id":1217,"title":"AFP installs new Camp Commander","slug":"afp-installs-new-camp-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 AFP installs new Camp Commander.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 AFP installs new Camp Commander.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomed the new Commander of General Headquarters and Headquarters Service Command (GHQ &amp; HSC) on Monday, April 11.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brigadier General Ferdinand S Razalan assumed the position from the outgoing Commander, Brigadier General George Joel N Lalaquil.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04122022%20AFP%20installs%20new%20Camp%20Commander.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-12T10:57:36+08:00","hits":381},{"id":1218,"title":"Troops clash with NPAs, firearms seized in Samar","slug":"troops-clash-with-npas-firearms-seized-in-samar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 Troops clash with NPAs firearms seized in Samar.jpg\" width=\"854\" height=\"384\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 Troops clash with NPAs firearms seized in Samar.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) troops figured in an intense firefight against communist New People’s Army terrorists (CNTs) in Samar on Sunday, April 10.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A squad from the Philippine Army’s 87th Infantry Battalion, while conducting combat security patrol, encountered more or less four CNTs in Brgy. Can-aponte, San Jose de Buan, Samar.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04122022%20Troops%20clash%20with%20NPAs%20firearms%20seized%20in%20Samar.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-12T10:51:53+08:00","hits":184},{"id":1219,"title":"AFP joins 80th Araw ng Kagitingan Anniversary","slug":"afp-joins-80th-araw-ng-kagitingan-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 AFP joins 80th Araw ng Kagitingan Anniversary.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 AFP joins 80th Araw ng Kagitingan Anniversary.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the 80th Araw ng Kagitingan anniversary celebration at Mount Samat National Shrine in Pilar, Bataan today, April 9.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Department of Justice Secretary Menardo Guevarra led the wreath-laying ceremony as respect and tribute to World War II heroes who defended the country's freedom. He was joined by His Excellency Koshikawa Kazuhiko, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Embassy of Japan; and Ms. Heather Variava, Chargé d'Affaires of the Embassy of the United States. Lieutenant General Ernesto Torres Jr, the Commander of AFP Northern Luzon Command, served as the military host.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04092022%20AFP%20joins%2080th%20Araw%20ng%20Kagitingan%20Anniversary.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-09T10:49:30+08:00","hits":279},{"id":1220,"title":"1 NPA terrorist killed in Bukidnon encounter","slug":"1-npa-terrorist-killed-in-bukidnon-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 1 NPA terrorist killed in Bukidnon encounter.jpg\" width=\"641\" height=\"855\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 1 NPA terrorist killed in Bukidnon encounter.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - One communist NPA terrorist (CNT) killed in an encounter with AFP troops in Malaybalay City, Bukidnon on March 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Lt. Col. Anthony Bacus, Commanding Officer of the Philippine Army's 8th Infantry Battalion under 403rd Infantry Brigade of the 4th Infantry Division, his troops responded to a report that an armed men were extorting money and farm produce from farmers when they encountered about 20 CNTs at Sitio Bendum, Brgy Busdi, Malaybalay City Bukidnon on Friday morning.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04092022%201%20NPA%20terrorist%20killed%20in%20Bukidnon%20encounter.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-09T10:45:41+08:00","hits":279},{"id":1221,"title":"AFP, PNP, PCG brace for 2022 Elections, sign operational guidelines on security","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-brace-for-2022-elections-sign-operational-guidelines-on-security","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 AFP PNP PCG brace for 2022 Elections sign operational guidelines on security.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"403\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04092022 AFP PNP PCG brace for 2022 Elections sign operational guidelines on security.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chiefs of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Philippine National Police (PNP), and Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) met with the Commission on Elections (COMELEC) to discuss security preparations for the coming National and Local Elections on Friday, April 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino, PNP Chief Police General Dionardo B Carlos, PCG Commandant Admiral Artemio M Abu, and COMELEC Chairman Saidamen Balt Pangarungan attended the third Joint Command Conference at the AFP Commissioned Officers Club in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04092022%20AFP%20PNP%20PCG%20brace%20for%202022%20Elections%20sign%20operational%20guidelines%20on%20security.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-09T10:42:42+08:00","hits":488},{"id":1222,"title":"Philippine, U.S. Forces Conclude 37th Exercise Balikatan","slug":"philippine-u-s-forces-conclude-37th-exercise-balikatan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04082022 New Attack Helicopters C-295 aircraft turned over to AFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04082022 New Attack Helicopters C-295 aircraft turned over to AFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Members of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the U.S. military successfully completed the 37th iteration of the Exercise Balikatan on Friday, April 8.</p>\r\n<p>Nearly 9,000 Filipino and American service members trained shoulder-to-shoulder from the northern coast of Luzon to Palawan over the last two weeks, focusing on maritime security, amphibious operations, live-fire training, urban operations, aviation operations, counterterrorism, and humanitarian assistance and disaster response.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04082022%20New%20Attack%20Helicopters%20C-295%20aircraft%20turned%20over%20to%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-08T17:15:51+08:00","hits":250},{"id":1223,"title":"4 terrorists killed, 16 firearms seized in Bukidnon encounter","slug":"4-terrorists-killed-16-firearms-seized-in-bukidnon-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 4 terrorists killed 16 firearms seized in Bukidnon encounter.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 4 terrorists killed 16 firearms seized in Bukidnon encounter.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Four high-ranking leaders of the Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) were killed in a decisive encounter with the Philippine Army's 1st Special Forces Battalion (1SFBn) in KM24, Barangay Tikalaan, Talakag, Bukidnon, on April 6.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lt. Gen. Greg T. Almerol, Commander of Eastern Mindanao Command, describes the operation as \"a major strike against the terrorist remnants.\"</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04072022%204%20terrorists%20killed%2016%20firearms%20seized%20in%20Bukidnon%20encounter.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-07T17:13:28+08:00","hits":306},{"id":1224,"title":"AFP weakens NPA firepower, discovers arms cache in Pampanga","slug":"afp-weakens-npa-firepower-discovers-arms-cache-in-pampanga","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 AFP weakens NPA firepower discovers arms cache in Pampanga.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"1067\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 AFP weakens NPA firepower discovers arms cache in Pampanga.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) continues to weaken the communist terrorist group's (CTG's) firepower as government troops seized an arms cache in Pampanga on April 7.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Joint elements of the 7th Infantry Division (7ID), Philippine Army's 70th Infantry Battalion, and Pampanga Provincial Police Station discovered the high-powered firearms at Barangay Ebus in Guagua, Pampanga.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04072022%20AFP%20weakens%20NPA%20firepower%20discovers%20arms%20cache%20in%20Pampanga.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-07T16:37:42+08:00","hits":251},{"id":1225,"title":"New Attack Helicopters, C-295 aircraft turned over to AFP","slug":"new-attack-helicopters-c-295-aircraft-turned-over-to-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 New Attack Helicopters C-295 aircraft turned over to AFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04072022 New Attack Helicopters C-295 aircraft turned over to AFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Two new T-129 “ATAK” Helicopters from Turkey and a C-295 Medium Lift Aircraft from Spain were officially turned over to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Wednesday, April 6.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The joint turn-over and blessing ceremony of the newly-acquired air assets was held at the 250th Presidential Airlift Wing Hangar in Villamor Airbase, Pasay City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04072022%20New%20Attack%20Helicopters%20C-295%20aircraft%20turned%20over%20to%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-07T16:35:07+08:00","hits":326},{"id":1226,"title":"266 NPAs surrender to AFP in 2022, more gains bared","slug":"266-npas-surrender-to-afp-in-2022-more-gains-bared-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) continues to degrade the Communist New People's Army Terrorists (CNTs) as 266 members surrendered to government forces from January to March 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most of the surrenders came from NPA units in Eastern Mindanao, with 114. Meanwhile, 58 fighters were from NPA units in Western Mindanao; 37 in Southern Luzon; 36 in the Visayas; 20 in Northern Luzon; and one from Palawan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-06T16:31:08+08:00","hits":351},{"id":1227,"title":"31 BIFF and ASG terrorists yield in Western Mindanao","slug":"31-biff-and-asg-terrorists-yield-in-western-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 31 BIFF and ASG terrorists yield in Western Mindanao.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 31 BIFF and ASG terrorists yield in Western Mindanao.jpg\" /></p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04052022%2031%20BIFF%20and%20ASG%20terrorists%20yield%20in%20Western%20Mindanao.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-05T16:19:15+08:00","hits":200},{"id":1228,"title":"AFP inks Agreement with Human Rights Group","slug":"afp-inks-agreement-with-human-rights-group","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 AFP inks Agreement with Human Rights Group.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"535\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 AFP inks Agreement with Human Rights Group.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) entered into a memorandum of understanding (MOU) with the Sulong Peace Incorporated (SPI) to advance human rights advocacies on Tuesday, April 5.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres C Centino, signed the agreement in a ceremony held at the General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo. Representing the SPI was Ms. Joeven Reyes-Escober, Executive Director.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04052022%20AFP%20inks%20Agreement%20with%20Human%20Rights%20Group.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-05T16:15:55+08:00","hits":335},{"id":1229,"title":"AFP renders Military Honors to World War II Veteran","slug":"afp-renders-military-honors-to-world-war-ii-veteran","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 AFP renders Military Honors to World War II Veteran.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"1197\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 AFP renders Military Honors to World War II Veteran.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) rendered military honors to World War II Veteran and Centenarian Juan Aquino Jacob, who passed away less than a month shy of his 102nd birthday.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Private Jacob, who died on March 27, 2022, was given final tribute and honors befitting a hero at the Libingan Ng Mga Bayani in Taguig City on April 2, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04052022%20AFP%20renders%20Military%20Honors%20to%20World%20War%20II%20Veteran.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-05T16:13:39+08:00","hits":278},{"id":1230,"title":"P3.95 Million Cash Assistance, Ambulance Bikes donated to AFP","slug":"p3-95-million-cash-assistance-ambulance-bikes-donated-to-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 P3.95 Million Cash Assistance Ambulance Bikes donated to AFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"620\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04052022 P3.95 Million Cash Assistance Ambulance Bikes donated to AFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received P3.95-Million financial assistance and various equipment from the MVP Group of Companies on Monday, April 4.<br /><br />AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino received the donations on behalf of the AFP during the handover ceremony at the General Headquarters canopy area in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04052022%20P3.95%20Million%20Cash%20Assistance%20Ambulance%20Bikes%20donated%20to%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-05T16:09:24+08:00","hits":267},{"id":1231,"title":"AFP completes New Home for Corps of Professors","slug":"afp-completes-new-home-for-corps-of-professors","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 AFP completes New Home for Corps of Professors.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 AFP completes New Home for Corps of Professors.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – After years of delay due to the pandemic, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) finally inaugurated the newly-constructed Corps of Professors Building in Camp Aguinaldo on Monday, April 4.</p>\r\n<p>The two-storey building will serve as the Office of the Dean, Corps of Professors, AFP (ODCOP, AFP) led by Colonel Stephen V Agtoto. It was a project passed down to him by former deans and pioneering members of the ODCOP, AFP headed by Brigadier General Archimedes Viaje in 2011.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04042022%20AFP%20completes%20New%20Home%20for%20Corps%20of%20Professors.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-04T16:06:43+08:00","hits":778},{"id":1232,"title":"AFP affirms commitment to ASEAN Security Cooperation","slug":"afp-affirms-commitment-to-asean-security-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 AFP affirms commitment to ASEAN Security Cooperation.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 AFP affirms commitment to ASEAN Security Cooperation.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) affirmed its commitment to ASEAN security cooperation during the 19th ASEAN Chiefs of Defence Forces Meeting-19 (ACDFM-19) in the Ministry of Defense, Phnom Penh, Cambodia, from 16-18 March 2022.</p>\r\n<p>The ACDFM is a meeting of Chiefs of Defense of ASEAN member countries that serves as a venue to strategically and comprehensively discuss and assess prominent issues of mutual interests related to common security challenges. It is also a venue for discussions on concerns raised during the ASEAN Summit and the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04042022%20AFP%20affirms%20commitment%20to%20ASEAN%20Security%20Cooperation.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-04T15:53:42+08:00","hits":460},{"id":1233,"title":"3 NPA's militia yield to AFP in Davao de Oro","slug":"3-npas-militia-yield-to-afp-in-davao-de-oro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 3 NPAs militia yield to AFP in Davao de Oro.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04042022 3 NPAs militia yield to AFP in Davao de Oro.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Three communist NPA terrorists (CNTs) militia or milisyang bayan (MB) surrendered to 89th Infantry Battalion (89IB) under the 1003rd Brigade of the Philippine Army's 10th Infantry Division (10ID) in Davao de Oro on weekend, April 3.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Military's sincerity and delivery of better government services are the reasons Alias Rustom, Alias Jomar, and Alias Justin (true name withheld for their security) when they surrendered to the soldiers of 89IB in Sitio Peroy Barangay Dagohoy, Talaingod, Davao de Oro. They belonged to the Subregional Guerilla Unit (SRGU), Subregional Committee Five (SRC5) of the NPA's Southern Mindanao Regional Committee (SMRC).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04042022%203%20NPAs%20militia%20yield%20to%20AFP%20in%20Davao%20de%20Oro.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-04T15:48:52+08:00","hits":335},{"id":1234,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff to SOCOM troops: Enhance Warfighting Skills","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-to-socom-troops-enhance-warfighting-skills","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04022022 AFP Chief of Staff to SOCOM troops Enhance Warfighting Skills.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04022022 AFP Chief of Staff to SOCOM troops Enhance Warfighting Skills.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Andres C Centino encouraged members of the Special Operations Command (SOCOM) to seek out new ways to enhance their warfighting skills.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“I encourage everyone to not only do a great job but also expand your horizons by overcoming your own limits. I am sure that through the guidance of your commander, you will continuously work on the perfection of your core competency that is warfighting which has surely contributed much to the mission accomplishment of the AFP,” he said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04022022%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20to%20SOCOM%20troops%20Enhance%20Warfighting%20Skills.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-02T15:45:26+08:00","hits":311},{"id":1235,"title":"8 Abu Sayyaf Group members surrender to AFP in Sulu","slug":"8-abu-sayyaf-group-members-surrender-to-afp-in-sulu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04012022 8 Abu Sayyaf Group members surrender to AFP in Sulu.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"771\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04012022 8 Abu Sayyaf Group members surrender to AFP in Sulu.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City - Eight Abu Sayyaf Group (ASG) members abandoned their armed struggle and submitted themselves to the military in Sulu on Thursday morning, March 31.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The surrenderees were presented to Maj. Gen. Ignatius Patrimonio, Commander of Joint Task Force Sulu and members of Talipao Municipal Task Force to End Local Armed Conflict (MTF-ELAC) at Talipao Municipal Hall, Barangay Bilaan, Talipao, Sulu.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04012022%208%20Abu%20Sayyaf%20Group%20members%20surrender%20to%20AFP%20in%20Sulu.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-01T15:40:00+08:00","hits":353},{"id":1236,"title":"AFP acquires Short Sherpa transport aircraft","slug":"afp-acquires-short-sherpa-transport-aircraft","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04012022 AFP acquires Short Sherpa transport aircraft.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04012022 AFP acquires Short Sherpa transport aircraft.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) acquired a Short Sherpa military transport aircraft previously owned by the Semirara Mining and Power Corporation on Friday, April 1.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Short Brothers &amp; Harland SD3-30 Aircraft was turned over to the Philippine Army in a ceremony held at the Ninoy Aquino International Airport, Pasay City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04012022%20AFP%20acquires%20Short%20Sherpa%20transport%20aircraft.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-01T15:37:21+08:00","hits":455},{"id":1237,"title":"AFP, U.S. Military hold Balikatan's Combined Arms Live Fire Exercise in Tarlac","slug":"afp-u-s-military-hold-balikatans-combined-arms-live-fire-exercise-in-tarlac","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 AFP U.S. Military hold Balikatans Combined Arms Live Fire Exercise in Tarlac.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"452\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 AFP U.S. Military hold Balikatans Combined Arms Live Fire Exercise in Tarlac.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Filipino and American service members successfully completed the Combined Arms Live Fire Exercises (CALFEX) at Colonel Ernesto Ravina Air Base in Capas, Tarlac on Thursday, March 31. </p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The CALFEX was among the highlights of this year’s Balikatan Exercises being conducted by the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and United States Indo-Pacific Command from March 28 to April 8, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03312022%20AFP%20U.S.%20Military%20hold%20Balikatans%20Combined%20Arms%20Live%20Fire%20Exercise%20in%20Tarlac.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-31T15:21:30+08:00","hits":249},{"id":1238,"title":"PH, US Conduct Balikatan's Amphibious Exercise in Cagayan Valley","slug":"ph-us-conduct-balikatans-amphibious-exercise-in-cagayan-valley","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 PH US Conduct Balikatans Amphibious Exercise in Cagayan Valley.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 PH US Conduct Balikatans Amphibious Exercise in Cagayan Valley.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Philippine and United States armed forces conducted a bilateral amphibious exercise (AMPHIBEX) on March 31, 2022 in the vicinity of Claveria, Cagayan Valley as part of the 37th iteration of Philippine-US Exercise Balikatan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AMPHIBEX involves the movement of assault amphibious vehicles (AAVs) from L-class ships to shore. It requires the vertical insertion of troops using different air assets of both armed forces. The activity demonstrated the bilateral force’s ability to seize a littoral objective as part of a complex, combined arms operations between Philippine and US ground, naval, and aviation assets.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03312022%20PH%20US%20Conduct%20Balikatans%20Amphibious%20Exercise%20in%20Cagayan%20Valley.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-31T15:18:06+08:00","hits":306},{"id":1239,"title":"Balikatan 2022 benefits schools in Cagayan and Isabela","slug":"balikatan-2022-benefits-schools-in-cagayan-and-isabela","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 Balikatan 2022 benefits schools in Cagayan and Isabela.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"626\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 Balikatan 2022 benefits schools in Cagayan and Isabela.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO QUEZON CITY- Four learning facilities at different schools in Cagayan and Isabela are being built by combined troops of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States Indo-Pacific Command under the Engineering Civic Action Projects (ENCAP) of the Balikatan 37-2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The construction of the buildings kicked off with a simultaneous groundbreaking ceremony on March 7, 2022. Troops aim to finish building the facilities towards the end of the Balikatan Exercises.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03312022%20Balikatan%202022%20benefits%20schools%20in%20Cagayan%20and%20Isabela.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-31T13:50:26+08:00","hits":233},{"id":1240,"title":" 12 BIFF members yield to AFP in Maguindanao","slug":"12-biff-members-yield-to-afp-in-maguindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 12 BIFF members yield to AFP in Maguindanao.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 12 BIFF members yield to AFP in Maguindanao.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City - Twelve Bangsamoro Islamic Freedom Fighters (BIFF), including a sub-leader and his deputy, decided to abandon their armed struggle and return to the fold of the law in Maguindanao on March 30, 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Lt. Gen. Alfredo Rosario Jr., Commander of the AFP's Western Mindanao Command (WESTMINCOM), Anwar Pegas, a sub-leader of the BIFF-Karialan Faction; Zukarno Sailila, his deputy; and 10 of their followers voluntarily surrendered to Lt. Col. Edwin Alburo, Commanding Officer of the 40th Infantry Battalion (40IB) at 40IB headquarters in Barangay Kabengi, Datu Saudi Ampatuan, Maguindanao.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03312022%2012%20BIFF%20members%20yield%20to%20AFP%20in%20Maguindanao.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-31T13:45:19+08:00","hits":254},{"id":1241,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff urges soldiers to be always at their best","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-urges-soldiers-to-be-always-at-their-best","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 AFP Chief of Staff urges soldiers to be always at their best.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03312022 AFP Chief of Staff urges soldiers to be always at their best.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino enjoins all soldiers to always be in shape and to be at their best in performing their mandate of protecting the people and securing the state.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his visit to the Joint Task Force – National Capital Region (JTF-NCR) under Brig. General Marceliano Teofilo on March 30, General Centino commended the military and civilian personnel of the JTF-NCR for successfully performing their mandate and pressed them to perform at their highest level.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03312022%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20urges%20soldiers%20to%20be%20always%20at%20their%20best.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T15:04:31+08:00","hits":246},{"id":1242,"title":"PH-US Military Free Fallers conduct Balikatan Friendship Jump","slug":"ph-us-military-free-fallers-conduct-balikatan-friendship-jump","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  PH-US Military Free Fallers conduct Balikatan Friendship Jump.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  PH-US Military Free Fallers conduct Balikatan Friendship Jump.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO QUEZON CITY- A total of 251 Special Operations Forces Military Free Faller and Airborne qualified from major special operations forces in connection to Balikatan 37-2022 conducted a Friendship Jump on March 28 and 29, 2022. This is part of the Combined Interoperability Events of the Combine Joint Special Operation Forces of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States Indo- Pacific Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03302022%20%20PH-US%20Military%20Free%20Fallers%20conduct%20Balikatan%20Friendship%20Jump.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T13:33:12+08:00","hits":266},{"id":1243,"title":"PH-US Military Forces build learning facility in Cagayan","slug":"ph-us-military-forces-build-learning-facility-in-cagayan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  PH-US Military Forces build learning facility in Cagayan.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  PH-US Military Forces build learning facility in Cagayan.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY – Combined troops of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States Indo-Pacific Command are currently building a school facility in Masi Elementary School, Rizal, Cagayan as part of the Engineering Civic Action Project (ENCAP) of the Balikatan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03302022%20%20PH-US%20Military%20Forces%20build%20learning%20facility%20in%20Cagayan.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T11:12:53+08:00","hits":219},{"id":1244,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff joins Peace Covenant Signing in Samar","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-joins-peace-covenant-signing-in-samar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  AFP Chief of Staff joins Peace Covenant Signing in Samar.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  AFP Chief of Staff joins Peace Covenant Signing in Samar.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - To reaffirm the military’s commitment to a secure and peaceful national and local elections, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined other participants in the Peace Covenant signing held at the 8th Infantry Division headquarters in Camp General Vicente Lukban, Catbalogan, Samar on March 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“I commit to our people that as Chief of Staff of the AFP, we will ensure credible and safe elections as directed by President Rodrigo Duterte. We will be there to assure that you will be safe and secure on election day,” AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03302022%20%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20joins%20Peace%20Covenant%20Signing%20in%20Samar.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T11:07:27+08:00","hits":324},{"id":1245,"title":"11 Abu Sayyaf in Basilan surrender to the AFP","slug":"11-abu-sayyaf-in-basilan-surrender-to-the-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  11 Abu Sayyaf in Basilan surrender to the AFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  11 Abu Sayyaf in Basilan surrender to the AFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City – Basilan-based Abu Sayyaf Group (ASG) members headed by notorious ASG sub-leader Abdullah Indanan surrendered to the Joint Task Force (JTF) Basilan / 101st Inf Bde on March 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Lt. Gen. Alfredo Rosarrio, Jr., Commander of Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM), ASG sub-leader Abdullah Indanan, a.k.a. Guro and ten other ASG members submitted themselves to JTF Basilan Commander, Brig. Gen. Domingo Gobway in Barangay Serongon, Hadji Mohammad Ajul, Basilan. This faction of the ASG operates in Lamitan-Tuburan-Mohammad Adjul complex.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03302022%20%2011%20Abu%20Sayyaf%20in%20Basilan%20surrender%20to%20the%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T10:40:22+08:00","hits":390},{"id":1246,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff awards medals to Army troops in Samar for gallantry in action against Communist Terrorists","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-awards-medals-to-army-troops-in-samar-for-gallantry-in-action-against-communist-terrorists","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  AFP Chief of Staff awards medals to Army troops in Samar for gallantry in action against Communist Terrorists.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03302022  AFP Chief of Staff awards medals to Army troops in Samar for gallantry in action against Communist Terrorists.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - For gallantry in action against the communist terrorist group (CTG), four Army troopers were awarded by the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff, Tuesday in Samar.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Andres C Centino, AFP Chief of Staff conferred the Gold Cross Medals to 1st Lieutenant Adonis Collado, Sergeant Vincent Bulan, and Corporal Ernesto Nuñez in a ceremony held at the 8th Infantry Division headquarters in Catbalogan, Samar.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03302022%20%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20awards%20medals%20to%20Army%20troops%20in%20Samar%20for%20gallantry%20in%20action%20against%20Communist%20Terrorists.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-30T10:37:21+08:00","hits":422},{"id":1247,"title":"9 NPAs yield, 30 firearms surrendered to AFP","slug":"9-npas-yield-30-firearms-surrendered-to-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03282022   Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan 2022 officially opens.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03282022   Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan 2022 officially opens.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Nine former members of the New People’s Army (NPA) guerilla front operating in Samar were presented to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Tuesday, March 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The relentless combat and non-combat operations of the Army’s 8th Infantry Division resulted in the surrender of Normie Quilapio, vice commander; and Adelfa Tebrero, political guide of Guerilla Front Damol, along with seven other members.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03282022%20%20%20Philippines-United%20States%20Exercise%20Balikatan%202022%20officially%20opens.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-28T10:34:24+08:00","hits":286},{"id":1248,"title":" Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan 2022 officially opens","slug":"philippines-united-states-exercise-balikatan-2022-officially-opens","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03282022   Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan 2022 officially opens.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03282022   Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan 2022 officially opens.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The 37th iteration of the Philippines-United States Exercise Balikatan was officially opened in a ceremony held at the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Headquarters on Monday, March 28.</p>\r\n<p>The 3,800 AFP and 5,100 United States Military members will participate in the combined joint exercises across the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03282022%20%20%20Philippines-United%20States%20Exercise%20Balikatan%202022%20officially%20opens.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-28T10:30:49+08:00","hits":411},{"id":1249,"title":"AFP welcomes new Education, Training and Doctrines Chief","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-education-training-and-doctrines-chief-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03252022  AFP welcomes new Education Training and Doctrines Chief.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03252022  AFP welcomes new Education Training and Doctrines Chief.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomed Commodore Donn Anthony L Miraflor as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training, and Doctrine (J8) on Thursday, March 24.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, presided over the Change of Chief of Office ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03252022%20%20AFP%20welcomes%20new%20Education%20Training%20and%20Doctrines%20Chief.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-25T10:24:59+08:00","hits":671},{"id":1250,"title":"Largest-ever Balikatan exercise set to begin in Philippines","slug":"largest-ever-balikatan-exercise-set-to-begin-in-philippines","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03222022  Largest-ever Balikatan exercise set to begin in Philippines.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03222022  Largest-ever Balikatan exercise set to begin in Philippines.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Approximately 8,900 members of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the U.S. military are teaming up for Balikatan 2022, the largest-ever iteration of the Philippine-led annual exercise taking place across Luzon, Mar. 28 to Apr. 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 3,800 AFP members and 5,100 U.S. military personnel will train shoulder-to-shoulder focusing on maritime security, amphibious operations, live-fire training, urban operations, aviation operations, counterterrorism, and humanitarian assistance and disaster relief.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03222022%20%20Largest-ever%20Balikatan%20exercise%20set%20to%20begin%20in%20Philippines.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-22T10:18:55+08:00","hits":276},{"id":1251,"title":"Exit Call of Defense Attaché of Turkey","slug":"exit-call-of-defense-attache-of-turkey","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03202022  Exit Call of Defense Attach of Turkey.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"594\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03202022  Exit Call of Defense Attach of Turkey.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>Capt Lemi Zik, Defense Attaché of Turkey to the Philippines, made an exit call to the acting Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Lieutenant General Erickson R Gloria, the AFP Vice Chief of Staff at the General Headquarters Building, Camp Aguinaldo on March 22.</p>\r\n<p>Capt Zik started his exit call to key officials of the AFP before his term as defense attaché ends on March 31. He is set to meet with the commanders of the Philippine Army, Philippine Air Force, and Philippine Navy, as well as the Secretary of National Defense.///(Photos by A2C Ted Castro PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202022/03202022%20%20Exit%20Call%20of%20Defense%20Attach%20of%20Turkey.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-20T10:07:02+08:00","hits":340},{"id":1252,"title":"3 terrorist NPAs killed, 1 captured in encounter with AFP in NorMin","slug":"3-terrorist-npas-killed-1-captured-in-encounter-with-afp-in-normin","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2022/03202022  3 terrorist NPAs killed 1 captured in encounter with AFP in NorMin.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2022/03202022  3 terrorist NPAs killed 1 captured in encounter with AFP in NorMin.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Three members of the communist NPA terrorists (CNTs) were killed, one captured in an encounter with the soldiers of 58th Infantry battalion under the 4th Infantry Division, Philippine Army in Sitio Solana, Barangay Plaridel, Claveria, Misamis Oriental on March 18, at 7:05 a.m.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Soldiers were on combat operation when they encountered more or less seven CNTs believed to be members of Weakened Guerilla Front (WGF Huawei, Sub Regional Command (SRC)1, North Central Mindanao Regional Committee (NCMRC).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-20T09:45:06+08:00","hits":353},{"id":1253,"title":"39 Local Terrorists surrender to AFP in Maguindanao","slug":"39-local-terrorists-surrender-to-afp-in-maguindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Thirty-nine members of different local terrorist groups (LTGs) surrendered along with their firearms to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao on Friday, March 18.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 21 identified members of Bangsamoro Islamic Freedom Fighters (BIFF)-Bungos Faction, 12 from the BIFF-Karialan Faction, and six (6) from Dawlah Islamiya-Turaife Group voluntarily submitted themselves at the Headquarters, 6th Infantry Division, Philippine Army (6ID, PA) in Camp Siongco, Awang.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-19T10:19:52+08:00","hits":285},{"id":1254,"title":"36 Communist Terrorists surrender in Sultan Kudarat","slug":"36-communist-terrorists-surrender-in-sultan-kudarat","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY – Continuous efforts by the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) prompted 36 NPA members to surrender on March 18, 2022, in Brgy. Tibpuan, Lebak, Sultan Kudarat.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The former rebels voluntarily presented themselves to the members of the 37th Infantry Battalion (37IB) under the 6th Infantry Division, Philippine Army.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-19T09:29:38+08:00","hits":390},{"id":1255,"title":"AFP welcomes new Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence, J2","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-deputy-chief-of-staff-for-intelligence-j2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03162022  AFP welcomes new Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence J2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03162022  AFP welcomes new Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence J2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomed Major General Romulo A Manuel Jr PA as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence, J2 on Wednesday, March 16, 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Major General Manuel replaced Major General Alex Luna during the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony at the General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. He likewise received his second star rank following his assumption as the new J2. Vice Admiral Anthony SD Reyes PN, The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, presided over the ceremony.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03162022%20%20AFP%20welcomes%20new%20Deputy%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20for%20Intelligence%20J2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-16T09:12:06+08:00","hits":2098},{"id":1256,"title":"AFP Statement on Loyalty to the Constitution","slug":"afp-statement-on-loyalty-to-the-constitution","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is firm in its resolve to be loyal to the Constitution and the duly constituted authorities.</p>\r\n<p>The 145,000-strong soldiers, airmen, sailors, and marines of the AFP stand solid behind the chain-of-command.</p>\r\n<p>It is our responsibility to uphold integrity as we execute our duty to serve the nation.</p>\r\n<p>While the AFP respects the people’s freedom of expression, we do not and will not support extra legal means outside the constitution which we have sworn to protect including the sanctity of the electoral process.</p>\r\n<p>We continuously remind our troops to adhere to the rule of law and always obey the chain of command, whoever is seated as the Commander-in-Chief.</p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces will remain a professional organization that will not engage in partisan politics and will at all times put the interest of the nation before personal views and opinions.///</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-15T09:03:35+08:00","hits":861},{"id":1257,"title":"AFP Prepares for Safe, Peaceful Elections","slug":"afp-prepares-for-safe-peaceful-elections","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is planning to deploy personnel from various military headquarters to assist the government in securing a safe and peaceful election in May.</p>\r\n<p>Military personnel performing non-combat missions may be tapped to carry out election duties prior, during, and after the National and Local Elections on May 9, 2022. This is to allow the AFP to focus on its primary mission to defeat local armed threats.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-15T08:56:52+08:00","hits":830},{"id":1258,"title":"Ambassador to Saudi Arabia meets with AFP Chief of Staff","slug":"ambassador-to-saudi-arabia-meets-with-afp-chief-of-staff","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03142022  Ambassador to Saudi Arabia meets with AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"954\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03142022  Ambassador to Saudi Arabia meets with AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>His Excellency Adnan Alonto, Philippine Ambassador to The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, paid a courtesy call to the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Monday, March 14.</p>\r\n<p>General Centino received Ambassador Alonto at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p>They discussed the possibility of opening up a Defense and Armed Forces Attaché position in Saudi Arabia and opportunities to explore a defense cooperation agreement between the two countries.///(Photos by SN1 Donald Viluan PN/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03142022%20%20Ambassador%20to%20Saudi%20Arabia%20meets%20with%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-14T00:46:54+08:00","hits":424},{"id":1259,"title":" AFP joins ground-breaking, turnover of projects to former CPP-NPA members in Aklan","slug":"afp-joins-ground-breaking-turnover-of-projects-to-former-cpp-npa-members-in-aklan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022   AFP joins ground-breaking turnover of projects to former CPP-NPA members in Aklan.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"348\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022   AFP joins ground-breaking turnover of projects to former CPP-NPA members in Aklan.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) participated in the ground-breaking and turnover ceremony of various projects to former Communist Party of the Philippines – New People’s Army (CPP-NPA) members in Ibajay, Aklan on March 10, 2022.</p>\r\n<p>The Commander of the 3rd Infantry Division, Philippine Army Major General Benedict M Arevalo attended the activity at the Kapatiran Peace and Development Community (KPDC).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03112022%20%20%20AFP%20joins%20ground-breaking%20turnover%20of%20projects%20to%20former%20CPP-NPA%20members%20in%20Aklan.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-11T08:32:46+08:00","hits":359},{"id":1260,"title":"AFP Chief visits Army unit in Marawi, awards medals to troops","slug":"afp-chief-visits-army-unit-in-marawi-awards-medals-to-troops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022  AFP Chief visits Army unit in Marawi awards medals to troops.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022  AFP Chief visits Army unit in Marawi awards medals to troops.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) visited Kampo Ranao in Marawi City on Thursday, March 10 to personally congratulate troops for the successful military operations against the local terrorist group in Lanao del Sur.</p>\r\n<p>“I commend all operating troops for the successful operation against the Dawlah Islamiya-Maute terrorist group. This is part of our ongoing intensified campaign to defeat armed threats before the President steps down. Let us sustain and maximize our accomplishments towards the drive to end local terrorism,” General Andres Centino PA said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03112022%20%20AFP%20Chief%20visits%20Army%20unit%20in%20Marawi%20awards%20medals%20to%20troops.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-11T08:21:23+08:00","hits":443},{"id":1261,"title":" AFP Installs Sovereignty Marker in the Country's Southernmost Frontier","slug":"afp-installs-sovereignty-marker-in-the-countrys-southernmost-frontier","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022  AFP Installs Sovereignty Marker in the Countrys Southernmost Frontier.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"453\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03112022  AFP Installs Sovereignty Marker in the Countrys Southernmost Frontier.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) successfully established a sovereignty marker in Panggungan Island, Brgy Datu Baguinda Puti, Sitangkai, Tawi-Tawi, strengthening the country’s sovereign rights over its southernmost frontier.</p>\r\n<p>The Joint Task Force Tawi-Tawi / Naval Task Group Tawi-Tawi / 2nd Marine Brigade under its Commander, Brigadier General Romero T Racadio PN(M) led the historic event on March 7, 2022. The establishment of the said landmark is one of the significant milestones in the province's history as it formally established its solid assertion of the area located at the southernmost frontier of the country's archipelago.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03112022%20%20AFP%20Installs%20Sovereignty%20Marker%20in%20the%20Countrys%20Southernmost%20Frontier.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-11T08:16:29+08:00","hits":350},{"id":1262,"title":"AFP chief visits Western Mindanao Command, relays guidance to troops","slug":"afp-chief-visits-western-mindanao-command-relays-guidance-to-troops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03102022 AFP chief visits Western Mindanao Command relays guidance to troops.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03102022 AFP chief visits Western Mindanao Command relays guidance to troops.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Andres C Centino PA visited the headquarters of Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM) in Zamboanga City on Thursday, March 10, 2022.</p>\r\n<p>General Centino was received by WESMINCOM Commander, LtGen Alfredo V Rosario PA. He was accorded with military honors after which proceeded to the traditional Talk to Troops.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03102022%20AFP%20chief%20visits%20Western%20Mindanao%20Command%20relays%20guidance%20to%20troops.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-11T08:13:08+08:00","hits":260},{"id":1263,"title":"Donning of Ranks to Senior Officers","slug":"donning-of-ranks-to-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03102022 Donning of Ranks to Senior Officers.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03102022 Donning of Ranks to Senior Officers.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino led the donning of ranks ceremony to AFP generals and senior officers on March 9, 2022, at Tejeros Hall, Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03102022%20Donning%20of%20Ranks%20to%20Senior%20Officers.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-10T16:44:20+08:00","hits":617},{"id":1264,"title":"AFP Chief visits PH Navy, lauds modernization, recent HADR efforts","slug":"afp-chief-visits-ph-navy-lauds-modernization-recent-hadr-efforts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022 AFP AFP Chief visits PH Navy lauds modernization recent HADR efforts.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022 AFP AFP Chief visits PH Navy lauds modernization recent HADR efforts.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Gen. Andres Centino, visited the Philippine Navy (PN) at the Philippine Fleet Headquarters at Naval Base Heracleo Alano in Sangley Point, Cavite, on March 9.</p>\r\n<p>In his message during his \"talk to troops,\" Gen. Centino extolled the Navy's modernization efforts, sharing his insights on a recent visit to Western Command in Palawan where he had the opportunity to personally see how the Philippine Navy has progressed over the years.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03092022%20AFP%20AFP%20Chief%20visits%20PH%20Navy%20lauds%20modernization%20recent%20HADR%20efforts.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-10T08:05:47+08:00","hits":382},{"id":1265,"title":" British Ambassador pays Introductory call on CSAFP","slug":"british-ambassador-pays-introductory-call-on-csafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022  British Ambassador pays Introductory call on CSAFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022  British Ambassador pays Introductory call on CSAFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Her Majesty's Ambassador Laure Beaufils, British Ambassador to the Philippines, rendered an introductory call on AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo on Tuesday, 08 March 2022.</p>\r\n<p>During the meeting, both sides expressed the importance of developing cooperation, and discussed regional dynamics and bilateral opportunities between the Philippines and the United Kingdom.<br />(Photos by TSg Randulf D Obinque PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03092022%20%20British%20Ambassador%20pays%20Introductory%20call%20on%20CSAFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-09T16:40:57+08:00","hits":243},{"id":1266,"title":"French Ambassador, Military Commander visit AFP General Headquarters","slug":"french-ambassador-military-commander-visit-afp-general-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022 French Ambassador Military Commander visit AFP General Headquarters.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03092022 French Ambassador Military Commander visit AFP General Headquarters.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The French Ambassador to the Philippines Her Excellency Michele Boccoz and the Joint Force Commander of the French Armed Forces in the Asia-Pacific Rear Admiral Jean-Mathieu Rey visited the General Headquarters (GHQ) of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Tuesday, March 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ambassador Boccoz and Rear Admiral Rey were accorded with military honors as they paid a courtesy call to AFP Vice Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Erickson Gloria. The parties discussed regional dynamics, French military engagements in Asia, as well as cooperation between both countries’ armed forces towards a free and open Indo-Pacific.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03092022%20French%20Ambassador%20Military%20Commander%20visit%20AFP%20General%20Headquarters.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-09T16:35:46+08:00","hits":251},{"id":1267,"title":"AFP Chief visits Air Force Headquarters, opens Interoperability Exercise","slug":"afp-chief-visits-air-force-headquarters-opens-interoperability-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03082022 AFP Chief visits Air Force Headquarters opens Interoperability Exercise.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03082022 AFP Chief visits Air Force Headquarters opens Interoperability Exercise.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Andres C Centino PA made his first official visit as Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) at the Headquarters, Philippine Air Force (PAF) in Pasay City on March 8.</p>\r\n<p>The AFP Chief was rendered military honors at the Villamor Air Base, where he was received by PAF Commanding General, Maj. Gen. Connor Anthony Canlas. He was also conferred with the Honorary Expert Missile System Officer Badge.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03082022%20AFP%20Chief%20visits%20Air%20Force%20Headquarters%20opens%20Interoperability%20Exercise.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-08T16:32:12+08:00","hits":268},{"id":1268,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff visits troops in Pag-asa Island","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-visits-troops-in-pag-asa-island","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03062022 AFP Chief of Staff visits troops in Pag-asa Island.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03062022 AFP Chief of Staff visits troops in Pag-asa Island.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff Gen. Andres Centino visited the troops in Pag-asa Island in the municipality of Kalayaan on Friday, March 4, 2022.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff's visit aims to inspect military facilities, check troops’ morale, and ensure unit operational readiness to accomplish the AFP mission.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03062022%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20visits%20troops%20in%20Pag-asa%20Island.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-06T16:22:40+08:00","hits":243},{"id":1269,"title":"AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Palawan","slug":"afp-chief-inspects-military-facilities-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar 2023/03042022 AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Palawan.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Mar 2023/03042022 AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Palawan.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA inspected vital military and government facilities in Palawan on March 3, 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Centino visited the Headquarters of Joint Task Force Malampaya in El Nido, Palawan, responsible for safeguarding the Malampaya gas field. He also inspected the former Matinloc and Nido gas platforms also in Palawan, which is now manned by JTF Malampaya.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/03042022%20AFP%20Chief%20inspects%20military%20facilities%20in%20Palawan.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-04T16:19:55+08:00","hits":278},{"id":1270,"title":"Malacañang approves the designation, promotion of AFP senior officers","slug":"malacanang-approves-the-designation-promotion-of-afp-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - President Rodrigo Roa Duterte approved the new designations and promotions of Generals, Flag Officers, and other Senior Officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in a series of communications forwarded to the General Headquarters, Armed Forces of the Philippines here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-03-04T16:16:22+08:00","hits":665},{"id":1271,"title":"US Navy's USS TULSA renders port call in Manila","slug":"us-navys-uss-tulsa-renders-port-call-in-manila","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02262022 US Navys USS TULSA renders port call in Manila.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"515\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02262022 US Navys USS TULSA renders port call in Manila.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The United States Navy's littoral combat ship USS TULSA is in Manila since 24 February 2022 for a regular port call.</p>\r\n<p>The vessel was granted diplomatic clearance by the Department of Foreign Affairs and is currently undergoing replenishment and maintenance.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02262022%20US%20Navys%20USS%20TULSA%20renders%20port%20call%20in%20Manila.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-26T16:12:30+08:00","hits":311},{"id":1272,"title":"General Centino presides over Change of Chief of Office ceremony of the OTDCSAFP","slug":"general-centino-presides-over-change-of-chief-of-office-ceremony-of-the-otdcsafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02252022 Courtesy Call of USARPAC Commanding General.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02252022 Courtesy Call of USARPAC Commanding General.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Andres C Centino PA presides over the change of chief of office and retirement ceremony of the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP on Thursday, February 24 at Tejeros Hall in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02252022%20Courtesy%20Call%20of%20USARPAC%20Commanding%20General.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-25T15:24:28+08:00","hits":308},{"id":1273,"title":"Courtesy Call of USARPAC Commanding General","slug":"courtesy-call-of-usarpac-commanding-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02212022 Courtesy Call of USARPAC Commanding General.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"597\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02212022 Courtesy Call of USARPAC Commanding General.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - General Charles Flynn, the Commanding General of the United States Army Pacific (USARPAC), rendered a courtesy call to the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), General Andres C Centino PA, on Monday, February 21 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02212022%20Courtesy%20Call%20of%20USARPAC%20Commanding%20General.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-21T15:11:43+08:00","hits":356},{"id":1274,"title":"General Centino lauds troops on recent victories vs NPAs in Mindanao","slug":"general-centino-lauds-troops-on-recent-victories-vs-npas-in-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02172022 General Centino lauds troops on recent victories vs NPAs in Mindanao.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"518\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02172022 General Centino lauds troops on recent victories vs NPAs in Mindanao.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino lauded the accomplishments of field units in Eastern Mindanao during his visit on Wednesday, 16 February 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff visited the troops of the 1003rd Infantry Brigade in Bunawan District, Davao City, and the 403rd Infantry Brigade in Malaybalay City, Bukidnon which weakened the communist terrorist group (CTG) in their areas of operation.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02172022%20General%20Centino%20lauds%20troops%20on%20recent%20victories%20vs%20NPAs%20in%20Mindanao.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-17T15:07:46+08:00","hits":277},{"id":1275,"title":"CSAFP visits Gozar Air Station and Littoral Monitoring Station Cabra","slug":"csafp-visits-gozar-air-station-and-littoral-monitoring-station-cabra","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02112022 CSAFP visits Gozar Air Station and Littoral Monitoring Station Cabra.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02112022 CSAFP visits Gozar Air Station and Littoral Monitoring Station Cabra.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA inspected Gozar Air Station and Littoral Monitoring Station Cabra, monitoring and warning facilities of the Philippine Air Force and Navy respectively in Lubang, Occidental Mindoro on February 11, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02112022%20CSAFP%20visits%20Gozar%20Air%20Station%20and%20Littoral%20Monitoring%20Station%20Cabra.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-12T15:05:55+08:00","hits":579},{"id":1276,"title":"CSAFP visits SOLCOM and 203rd IB","slug":"csafp-visits-solcom-and-203rd-ib","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02112022 CSAFP visits SOLCOM and 203rd IB.jpg\" width=\"854\" height=\"569\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02112022 CSAFP visits SOLCOM and 203rd IB.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA visited Southern Luzon Command and 203rd Infantry Brigade in Lucena City, Quezon, and Bansud, Oriental Mindoro, respectively, on February 11, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02112022%20CSAFP%20visits%20SOLCOM%20and%20203rd%20IB.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-11T15:02:00+08:00","hits":402},{"id":1277,"title":"CESSNA Skyhawks turn-over and blessing","slug":"cessna-skyhawks-turn-over-and-blessing","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02102022 CESSNA Skyhawks turn-over and blessing.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02102022 CESSNA Skyhawks turn-over and blessing.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C. Centino PA joins Secretary of National Defense Delfin N Lorenzana in the formal acceptance, blessing, turnover, and activation of four Cessna 172S Skyhawk Trainer Aircrafts at Naval Base Heracleo Alano, Sangley Point, Cavite on Thursday, February 10, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02102022%20CESSNA%20Skyhawks%20turn-over%20and%20blessing.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-10T14:57:42+08:00","hits":290},{"id":1278,"title":"AFPSM Change of Chief of Office","slug":"afpsm-change-of-chief-of-office","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02102022 AFPSM Change of Chief of Office.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02102022 AFPSM Change of Chief of Office.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA presides over the Change of Chief of Office and Retirement Ceremony for the AFP Sergeant Major on Wednesday, February 9, 2022 at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. FCMS Aladin S Dacayanan PA, the highest-ranked Non-Commissioned Officer bowed out of service and was replaced by Master Chief Petty Officer Freddie E. Asence PN as the Acting AFPSM.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by TSg Obinque PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02102022%20AFPSM%20Change%20of%20Chief%20of%20Office.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-10T14:52:35+08:00","hits":477},{"id":1279,"title":"AFP receives military equipment from China","slug":"afp-receives-military-equipment-from-china","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02092022 AFP receives military equipment from China.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"573\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02092022 AFP receives military equipment from China.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Department of National Defense (DND) Secretary Delfin Lorenzana and the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA accepted the first batch of military equipment from the Ministry of National Defense (MND) of the People's Republic of China (PROC) today, February 9, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02092022%20AFP%20receives%20military%20equipment%20from%20China.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-09T14:43:18+08:00","hits":343},{"id":1280,"title":"AFP, PNP, PCG agree on legal cooperation vs threat groups","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-agree-on-legal-cooperation-vs-threat-groups","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02072022 AFP PNP PCG agree on legal cooperation vs threat groups.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02072022 AFP PNP PCG agree on legal cooperation vs threat groups.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines, the Philippine National Police, and the Philippine Coast Guard agreed to adopt a joint legal cooperation against threat groups by signing Joint Letter Directive (JLD) No. 01-2022 in connection with the upcoming National and Local Election 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02072022%20AFP%20PNP%20PCG%20agree%20on%20legal%20cooperation%20vs%20threat%20groups.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-07T14:35:15+08:00","hits":1038},{"id":1281,"title":"PLEDGE OF COMMITMENT","slug":"pledge-of-commitment","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02032022 PLEDGE OF COMMITMENT.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02032022 PLEDGE OF COMMITMENT.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA signs the manifesto affirming the AFP's commitment to help ensure a safe, accurate, free, and fair elections (SAFE) this year. General Centino was among the different government agency heads who joined the launching of KASIMBAYANAN and pledged support for SAFE in Camp Crame, Quezon City on Thursday, 03 February 2022. (Photo by SN1 VILUAN/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02032022%20PLEDGE%20OF%20COMMITMENT.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-03T14:29:04+08:00","hits":800},{"id":1282,"title":"General Centino lauds Diamond Division, pledges all-out support vs insurgency","slug":"general-centino-lauds-diamond-division-pledges-all-out-support-vs-insurgency","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2022/02022022 General Centino lauds Diamond Division.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2022/02022022 General Centino lauds Diamond Division.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-- The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines General Andres C Centino PA lauded the 4th Infantry (Diamond) Division for its accomplishments against the communist terrorist group.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his visit on Wednesday, 02 February 2022, General Centino pressed the troops to finish the insurgency in Northern Mindanao before June 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202022/02022022%20General%20Centino%20lauds%20Diamond%20Division.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-02-02T14:26:00+08:00","hits":414},{"id":1283,"title":"NEW INSPECTOR GENERAL","slug":"new-inspector-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01312022 NEW INSPECTOR GENERAL.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01312022 NEW INSPECTOR GENERAL.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines' Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA presides over the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony on Monday, 31 January 2022, at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  MGen William N Gonzales PA formally assumed as The Inspector General, replacing BGen Joseph Ferrous S Cuison PN(M) who served as the acting TIG since LtGen Franco Nemesio M Gacal retired on 08 December 2021. (Photo by SN1 Viluan/PAO, AFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01312022%20NEW%20INSPECTOR%20GENERAL.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-31T14:21:21+08:00","hits":737},{"id":1285,"title":"Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff General Lisandro Abadia","slug":"military-honors-for-the-late-former-afp-chief-of-staff-general-lisandro-abadia-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"ea70b\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01292022 Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01292022 Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" /></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) rendered traditional military funeral honors to its former Chief of Staff, General Lisandro Abadia on Saturday, January 29 at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani in Fort Bonifacio.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"ea70b\" data-offset-key=\"1p0ll-0-0\"> ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01292022%20Military%20honors%20for%20the%20late%20former%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-29T11:03:27+08:00","hits":652},{"id":1284,"title":"Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff General Lisandro Abadia","slug":"military-honors-for-the-late-former-afp-chief-of-staff-general-lisandro-abadia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"ea70b\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01292022 Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01292022 Military honors for the late former AFP Chief of Staff.jpg\" /></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"hqti-0-0\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) rendered traditional military funeral honors to its former Chief of Staff, General Lisandro Abadia on Saturday, January 29 at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani in Fort Bonifacio.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"ea70b\" data-offset-key=\"1p0ll-0-0\"> ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01292022%20Military%20honors%20for%20the%20late%20former%20AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-29T11:03:27+08:00","hits":449},{"id":1286,"title":"AFP Pushes to End Communist Insurgency  before Pres. Duterte’s Term Ends","slug":"afp-pushes-to-end-communist-insurgency-before-pres-duterte-s-term-ends","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01252022  AFP Pushes to End Communist Insurgency.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01252022  AFP Pushes to End Communist Insurgency.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — During its year-end Command Conference held at the AFP General Headquarters on 25 January 2022, the AFP leadership pushes to end the local communist insurgency by the time President Duterte’s term ends. With Major Services and Unified Commanders in attendance, AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino reiterated the AFP’s urgent and key tasks for 2022—to end local armed conflict and ensure a secure and peaceful 2022 National and Local Elections.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01252022%20%20AFP%20Pushes%20to%20End%20Communist%20Insurgency.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-25T10:59:52+08:00","hits":443},{"id":1287,"title":"AFP honors late CSAFP General Abadia","slug":"afp-honors-late-csafp-general-abadia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01252022 AFP honors late CSAFP General Abadia.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01252022 AFP honors late CSAFP General Abadia.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) accorded military honors to the late General Lisandro C Abadia, former AFP Chief of Staff on January 25, 2022. General Andres C Centino PA, the current AFP Chief of Staff welcomed the family and relatives of General Abadia at the General Headquarters (GHQ), Camp Aguinaldo where the former Chief of Staff’s cremains shall stay for public viewing until January 27.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01252022%20AFP%20honors%20late%20CSAFP%20General%20Abadia.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-25T10:56:51+08:00","hits":491},{"id":1288,"title":"NOLCOM Change of Command","slug":"nolcom-change-of-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01242022 NOLCOM Change of Command.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"548\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01242022 NOLCOM Change of Command.jpg\" />Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA presides over on Monday, 24 January 2022, the Change of Command Ceremony that formally installed LtGen Ernesto C Torres Jr PA as the new Commander of Northern Luzon Command. LtGen Torres replaced MGen Andrew Costelo PA who took over as acting commander following the retirement of LtGen Arnulfo Marcelo B Burgos Jr in December last year. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01202022%20WESCOM%20Change%20of%20Command.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-24T10:52:56+08:00","hits":583},{"id":1289,"title":"WESCOM Change of Command","slug":"wescom-change-of-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01202022 WESCOM Change of Command.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01202022 WESCOM Change of Command.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA presides over the Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony for outgoing Commander, Western Command (WESCOM) VAdm Ramil Roberto B Enriquez PN who bowed out of service after 38 years in the military. He was replaced by RAdm Alberto B Carlos PN in the ceremony held at the WESCOM Headquarters in Puerto Princesa, Palawan on 21 January 2022. (Photo by SN1 Viluan/PAO, AFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01202022%20WESCOM%20Change%20of%20Command.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-21T10:13:08+08:00","hits":518},{"id":1290,"title":"AFP receives donations from AFPMBAI","slug":"afp-receives-donations-from-afpmbai","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01202022 AFP receives donations from AFPMBAI.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01202022 AFP receives donations from AFPMBAI.jpg\" />The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received vehicles and various equipment from the Armed Forces and Police Mutual Benefit Association Inc. (AFPMBAI) on Thursday, January 20. AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA accepted the donations in a Turn-over Ceremony held at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. Among AFPMBAI's donations are ambulance, Toyota Coaster, gym and entertainment packages, and COVID-19 supplies.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos by SN1 Viluan PN/PAOAFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-20T10:09:39+08:00","hits":440},{"id":1291,"title":"AFP Statement on New Appointments","slug":"afp-statement-on-new-appointments","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomes the appointment of Major General Ernesto C Torres JR PA, Major General William N Gonzales PA, Major General Nestor C Herico PN(M), Rear Admiral Alberto B Carlos PN, and Rear Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes PN to AFP key positions as approved by President Rodrigo Roa Duterte.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-19T10:06:11+08:00","hits":627},{"id":1292,"title":"State Funeral for National Artist F. Sionil Jose","slug":"state-funeral-for-national-artist-f-sionil-jose","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01182022 State Funeral for National Artist F. Sionil Jose.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"527\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01182022 State Funeral for National Artist F. Sionil Jose.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) accorded honors to the late National Artist F. Sionil Jose on Tuesday, January 18. Colonel Jonathan Gayas PA, Deputy Army Adjutant served as the Military Host during the State Funeral and Interment Ceremony held at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by Sgt Manzano PA/PAOAFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01182022%20State%20Funeral%20for%20National%20Artist%20F.%20Sionil%20Jose.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-18T09:48:10+08:00","hits":781},{"id":1293,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff reports HADR accomplishments, receives praises from PRRD","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-reports-hadr-accomplishments-receives-praises-from-prrd","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines’ Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA reported to President Rodrigo Duterte the military’s accomplishments in its response to Typhoon Odette via video teleconferencing during the \"Talk to the People\" hosted by PRRD on 17 January 2022 from Davao City.</p>\r\n<p>“Our personnel were immediately deployed to help in the prevention, mitigation, and response operations before, during, and after the typhoon to assist in the delivery and transport of relief goods, supplies, equipment, and personnel in the affected areas,” General Centino said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-18T09:43:24+08:00","hits":429},{"id":1294,"title":"Chiefs of Defense Meeting","slug":"chiefs-of-defense-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01132022 Chiefs of Defense Meeting.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01132022 Chiefs of Defense Meeting.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA joins the virtual Chiefs of Defense Meeting on 13 January 2022. General Centino discussed the AFP's strategic priorities for 2022 in the meeting hosted by the US INDO-PACIFIC Command and attended by 24 top and senior military leaders from 24 countries. This event is a continuation of the primary Chiefs of Defense meeting held in August 2021 in Honolulu, Hawaii. (Photos by SN1 Viluan/PAO, AFP)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01132022%20Chiefs%20of%20Defense%20Meeting.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-13T09:38:21+08:00","hits":298},{"id":1295,"title":"AFP Statement on the Passing of Former Chief of Staff General Lisandro Abadia","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-passing-of-former-chief-of-staff-general-lisandro-abadia-3","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines extends its sincerest condolences to the family and friends of General Lisandro Abadia, former AFP Chief of Staff.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-10T09:33:50+08:00","hits":339},{"id":1296,"title":"AFP Statement on Chief of Staff, AFP testing Positive for COVID-19","slug":"afp-statement-on-chief-of-staff-afp-testing-positive-for-covid-19","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines confirms that the AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino has tested positive for COVID-19, yesterday.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-07T09:29:56+08:00","hits":358},{"id":1297,"title":"Number 1 Most Wanted CPP/NPA/NDF Leader in Mindanao killed","slug":"number-1-most-wanted-cpp-npa-ndf-leader-in-mindanao-killed-5","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">MAWAB, DAVAO DE ORO - Menandro Villanueva alias BOK, the longest-serving Secretary of Southern Mindanao Regional Committee (SMRC), currently the Secretary of Komisyong Mindanao (KOMMID), Commanding Officer of the NPA’s National Operations Command (NOC), and member of the POLITBURO of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of the Philippines (CPP) was killed in an encounter against the troops under 1001st Infantry Brigade at Brgy Libudon, Mabini, Davao de Oro on Wednesday evening, January 5, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-06T08:57:23+08:00","hits":743},{"id":1298,"title":"New Year's Message of the AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA","slug":"new-years-message-the-afp-chief-of-staff-general-andres-c-centino-pa","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/GEN_CENTINO.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/GEN_CENTINO.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>It is with immense pride and joy that I extend my felicitations to the gallant men and women of the Armed Forces of the Philippines as we welcome the New Year together as one big AFP family. A happy and blessed new year to one and all!</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/GEN_CENTINO.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-01T03:07:05+08:00","hits":1184},{"id":1299,"title":"AFP Mobile Kitchen in Cebu receives donations from San Miguel Foundation","slug":"afp-mobile-kitchen-in-cebu-receives-donations-from-san-miguel-foundation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2022/01012022 AFP Mobile Kitchen in Cebu receives donations from San Miguel Foundation.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2022/01012022 AFP Mobile Kitchen in Cebu receives donations from San Miguel Foundation.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) will use the canned goods worth P500,000 donated by San Miguel Foundation, Inc. to feed typhoon victims in Cebu Province through the AFP Mobile Kitchen.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202022/01012022%20AFP%20Mobile%20Kitchen%20in%20Cebu%20receives%20donations%20from%20San%20Miguel%20Foundation.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-01-01T00:45:02+08:00","hits":396},{"id":1300,"title":"Be a hero to our heroes' children in the 6th HERO Golf Cup","slug":"be-a-hero-to-our-heroes-children-in-the-6th-hero-golf-cup","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The HERO Golf Cup is an annual charity golf tournament organized by the HERO (Help Educate and Rear Orphans) Foundation, Inc. Now on its 6th year, all proceeds of the tournament will go to help fund the educational needs of orphaned children and dependent siblings of soldiers who were permanently incapacitated or killed due to enemy action or during disaster relief operations..</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Mar%202023/030323%20BE%20a%20Hero%20to%20our%20heroes.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2021-01-21T03:07:05+08:00","hits":415}]}